Dear all, 

a great thank to José Pinheiro who solved my problem straightfully.

1- my problem with varComb in the weights parameter of the nlme function was simply related to the fact that nlme library 3.3.1 was not attached before nlme3. This last one was dominant, and had a bug with varComb.

The simple solution is just to write somtehing like

> library(nlme331, first = T)

when attaching the library (and maybe also to detach nlme3, otherwise, you have a lot of warnings).

2- I submitted out of the list another problem to José, relative to a problem with a column in my dataset (groupedData) that was in "date" format: 

toto_groupedData(y~group|block/plot/subplot,data="">

# I now transfer all the columns of vsa1.1L, including column 19 in date format

mod.vsa1.1L.R.SU.stgu_nlme(y~lien.exp(a),fixed=a~group,data="">

