Problem in nlme.formula(y ~ lien.exp(a), fixed = a ~ group, data = "" ra..: Length of datv (variable 20) is 5 != length of 

others (6912)

Here is José's answer:

The second problem you reported indicated a bug in the code, related to how

the model frame used to evaluated the variables is being generated (all

variables are being used, instead of just the ones referenced in the model,

as it should be the case). There seems to be a problem in S-PLUS related to

the evaluation of date variables, but I didn't try to explore that avenue.

Anyway, I am attaching a corrected version of nlme.formula which you can

source into S-PLUS to fix the second problem. Notice that this function

