On Fri, 15 Mar 2002, Megan Pledger wrote:

> The problem you described in an earlier post was fitting models without
> intercepts. Are these the problems that you are referring to here? Or are
> there broader problems with stepwise()/stepAIC?

As author of stepAIC, I object to being tarred by the brush of unrelated
software.

Both stepwise() and step() have fundamental limitations not in stepAIC: in
particular step() does not compute Akaike's AIC, and is dangerous for use
with binomial and Poisson glms.  This is all well-documented over many
years (since 1992 as I recall: see V&R1 for example).

