On Fri, 15 Mar 2002, Ranjan Maitra wrote:

> Can someone please explain to me what the image color scheme
> specifications stands for. More specifically, I am in the Splus
> motif() window (Splus 6.0, Linux 6.2) and am looking at the Color
> Scheme Specifications which read, for Visible Light:
>
> red 8 yellow 8 green 8 cyan 8 blue 8 magenta
>
> What do these numbers mean? Does anyone know?

Someone does, as there is code to interpret them ....

This is about a specific device so I have changed the subject.

The named colours are colours known to X11, which has a mapping to RGB.
`man rgb' may tell you about it.  If `Linux 6.2' is RedHat 6.2,
`man showrgb' will do the trick.

The `8' means linearly interpolate 8 colours.   You will also see `h16',
which means interpolate 16 halftones.

