Hello,

 

I use S-plus 6 for windows.

 

I am trying to solve a non-linear equation in the 
following form in S-plus.

 

integrate (min(x^2/S^2, b^2) dF=C.

 

Here the integration is from negative infinite 
to positive infinite, b and C are constants, F is cumulative probability 
distribution(say, norm), S is variable.

 

I have tried the following code in S-plus, but 
there are some errors that I can not understand. And I am not sure whether it is 
the right way to solve it.

 

Is there anyone can help me with this problem? 
Any suggestions would be 
appreciated.

 

Thanks in advance.

 

Best Regards,

Haiyan Gao

----------------------------------------------------------------

          bend<-1.28; C<-0.67

psi.b<-function(x, b){ifelse(x < -b, 
-b,ifelse(x < b, x, b))}

integrand <- function(x, S) {(psi.b(x/S, bend))^2*dnorm(x, 
0,1)} 

f1<-function(S){substitute(integrate(integrand, lower = -Inf, upper = Inf, 
S=S)[[1]])-C}

uniroot(f1, 
c(0.5,100))

