Hi all

Thank you to Max Kuhn, Brad Biggerstaff, James McBroom, David Smith and
Frederic Gosselin  for their replies. The question was about contraining
parameters in non-linear estimation, in particular to non-negative values.
This can be done very simply. If we want parameter A to be non-normal then
we substitute exp(A1) for A in the formula when . Then we can simply take
the natural log of the estimate for A1 to get a (non-negative) estimate for
A. Frederic's helpful illustration is shown below: 

 If you wish that parameter a in 

y~exp(a+b*x) 

be positive. You can redefine your function in the following way: 

y~exp(exp(a)+b*x)

Thanks again to all who replied

