Dear Splus Users! I 
have a data.frame which contains 648 rows and 8 columns. One of the columns is 
an indicator variable (0-1). I would like to split this data.frame into 2 parts: 
one with indicator=1 and one with indicator=0. Is there exist a simple way to do 
it?  (There are 482 rows corresponding to indicator=0 and 166 rows 
corresponding to indicator=1 in original data frame). Thank you in advance for 
your help.  

 

 

I am working with Splus 45 on Windows. 

From sundard at PDF.COM  Tue Mar 26 15:08:38 2002
From: sundard at PDF.COM (Sundar Dorai-Raj)
Date: Tue, 26 Mar 2002 09:08:38 -0600
Subject: Re: splitting the data.frame
References: <003d01c1d4b6$c02b8ae0$3f0d4084@x9v4k5>
Message-ID: <3CA08EF6.2D2F1FBB@pdf.com>

split(data,data$indicator) 

produces a list with two elements: the first element will be the data
frame where data$indicator==0; the second element will be the data frame
where data$indicator==1. The dimension of the first element will be
{dim==c(482,8)} and the dimension of the second element will be
{dim==c(166,8)}.

Sundar

