Dear list

Thank you to Frederic Gosselin, Jacob W. Bowers and José Pinheiro for their
replies to my queries.

I asked about the cause of two error statements when attempting to model
hetersoscadesity under nlme. 

 I have
        > tried to fitted the following :
        >
        > sm98m3o.nlme.power9 <- update(sm98m3o.nlme.power7, weights =
varPower())
        >
        > But get the following error messages :
        >
        > Warning in ms( ~  - logLik(nlmeSt, nlmePars), start = list(: FALSE
        > CONVERGENCE.
        > Error in .C("mixed_loglik",: Singular precision matrix in level 1,
block

This error message can be the causes by different things. One possibility is
when the predicted values are close to zero.b In which case varConstPower
can be used instead. Another cause of convergence is there is a bug in older
version of nlme 3.0 . The most up to version 3.3.1 can be accessed at :
http://nlme.stat.wisc.edu <http://nlme.stat.wisc.edu>  . I found that
installing this version resolved some of my convergence problems. You can
check the version by looking in the library directory. If you install a
newer version you need to make the new library available. This can be done
by using the command : 
library(nlme, first = T) where nlme is the directory with the newer version
of nlme.

